r differential testing\n     - Need to run `go vet` and potentially tests to verify\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification with full project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, requirements, design decisions, acceptance criteria, and constraints for implementing seq edge cases and error handling (task #5173)\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Request to create a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/seq/main.go` to ensure all error handling and edge cases match GNU seq behavior\n   - Verify error message formats match GNU seq (especially the zero increment message)\n   - Ensure streaming works correctly for large sequences\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/seq/...` to verify compilation (AC6)\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC6 pass\n   - Do NOT run git commands (managed externally by orchestrator)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the two required files (`cmd/seq/main.go` and `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd019-seq.yaml`) and was about to plan and implement the changes. No code modifications have been made yet. The analysis phase was in progress — I was comparing the existing implementation against the task requirements to determine what changes are needed.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the required changes to `cmd/seq/main.go`. Based on analysis, the main changes likely needed are:\n   - Fix the zero increment error message format (line 54: `\"invalid Zero increment value: '%s'\"` → likely needs to match GNU format like `\"invalid Zero increment value: '%s'\"` or similar — need to check GNU behavior)\n   - Verify and potentially adjust error message wording to match GNU seq exactly for differential testing\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/seq/...` to verify AC6\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/seq/... -count=1` if tests exist\n   \n   The task description says: \"Handle large sequences, invalid arguments, argument count v