se the correct wording. I'm also noticing that GNU accepts \"inf\" and generates numbers forever, while our code rejects it with an error—that's another difference to consider.\n\nNow I'm updating the parseNumber function to handle these cases properly, with distinct error messages for NaN versus other invalid floating point values.\n\nWriting test file...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":34385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13f5bbc1-b2d8-4a91-bf97-10193c31abab","uuid":"2c584e7b-04de-4d1c-9c00-4b30f7b2ae61"}
